  "prompt": "For the checkout test AB-2025-01, compare the treatment variant with control. A customer converted in a variant when the customer has a conversion in the test at or after the customer's assigned_at for that variant; a customer who converted more than once counts once, and a customer assigned to both variants counts in each of them. A variant's conversion rate is 100 times its converted customers divided by its assigned customers. Return one row with four columns, in this order: control_rate_pct and treatment_rate_pct, the two conversion rates, each rounded to 2 decimals; abs_lift_pp, the absolute lift in percentage points, the treatment rate minus the control rate, rounded to 2 decimals; and rel_lift_pct, the relative lift in percent, 100 times the absolute lift divided by the control rate, rounded to 1 decimal. Work out both lifts from the unrounded rates. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "control_rate_pct",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "treatment_rate_pct",
